## Why This Is Asked
Tests that cover client-side persistence and recovery from autosave are common in product forms. This checks basic E2E skills without server integration.

## Key Concepts
- E2E testing of client-side autosave via localStorage
- Time control with cy.clock and cy.tick
- Form state restoration after reload
- Cleanup of autosave after completion

## Code Example
```javascript
describe('Profile Wizard Autosave', () => {
  it('restores autosaved progress after reload', () => {
    cy.clock();
    cy.visit('/profile/new');
    cy.get('#firstName').type('Alex');
    cy.tick(120000);
    cy.window().then(win => {
      const data = JSON.parse(win.localStorage.getItem('profile_wizard'));
      expect(data?.firstName).to.eq('Alex');
    });
    cy.reload();
    cy.get('#firstName').should('have.value', 'Alex');
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this test for multiple locales or browsers?
- How would you handle autosave failures or corrupted localStorage data?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests for autosave/drafts cover offline-first UX, idempotent writes, and cross-device conflicts, which are common pain points in real apps.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first data flows and write queuing
- Idempotent REST writes and ordering guarantees
- Test data isolation via seeds and reset hooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright skeleton (pseudo)
test('autosave offline queue and merge', async ({ page, request }) => {
  await page.goto('/editor');
  await page.fill('#note', 'Initial');
  await page.waitForTimeout(31000); // wait for autosave
  // simulate offline
  await page.route('POST', '/api/drafts', route => route.abort());
  await page.fill('#note', 'Offline edit');
  await page.setOfflineMode(true);
  await page.fill('#note', 'More offline edits');
  await page.setOfflineMode(false);
  // verify upload order and no duplicates
  // reload or inspect draft store
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for WebSocket-based drafting?
- How would you test long offline periods and partial merges?

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses a candidate's understanding of end-to-end testing for multi-step user journeys, including authentication flows, external system mocking, and deterministic test data management. It evaluates practical knowledge of creating reliable, fast, and isolated tests in a real-world SaaS context.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end testing with authentication and email verification
- Test data seeding and database isolation
- Mocking external services (email delivery, OIDC sign-in)
- Assertions for UI state and created resources
- Time-bounded test design for CI/CD pipelines

## Code Example

```javascript
// Using Playwright
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('complete onboarding flow', async ({ page }) => {
  // Seed deterministic test data
  await seedTestUser({ email: 'demo@test.com', password: 'Test123!' });

  // Mock email service to capture verification link
  await mockEmailService();

  // Mock OIDC provider
  await mockOIDCProvider();

  // Navigate to signup and complete registration
  await page.goto('/signup');
  await page.fill('[name=email]', 'demo@test.com');
  await page.fill('[name=password]', 'Test123!');
  await page.click('[data-testid=signup-submit]');

  // Extract and follow email verification link
  const verifyLink = await getVerificationLink('demo@test.com');
  await page.goto(verifyLink);

  // Complete profile setup
  await page.fill('[name=name]', 'Jane Doe');
  await page.fill('[name=company]', 'Acme Corp');
  await page.click('[data-testid=profile-submit]');

  // Create first workspace
  await page.fill('[name=workspaceName]', 'My Workspace');
  await page.click('[data-testid=create-workspace]');

  // Assert dashboard displays new workspace
  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid=workspace-card]')).toContainText('My Workspace');
});
```

